#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:41
msgid ""
"image:goblins/logo.webp[width=108,height=108,float=\"right\"] Goblins are "
"small, green, vicious, mean-spirited and generally unpleasant creatures. "
"Clues as to their character may be discerned in their tiny pointed teeth, "
"beady glinting eyes, scrawny grasping hands and general demeanour of a "
"whipped dog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:50
msgid ""
"To give them their due, Goblins are prolific. There are lots of them and no "
"matter how many die or run away, there are always plenty left. Their "
"preferred method of fighting is to shoot their enemy in the back from a good "
"distance. They are half-way decent shots but in other respects are poor and "
"often unwilling fighters. However, they are dangerous in large numbers and "
"quite capable of overwhelming far better troops by sheer weight of numbers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Like all greenskins, Goblins are quarrelsome and fractious.  They fight "
"amongst themselves both on and off the battlefield.  They feel little sense "
"of loyalty to their own kind let alone anyone else, and will cheerfully "
"maim, kill and even eat their comrades if they can get away with it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Goblins are generally recognised as belonging to two main breeds, namely "
"Common Goblins and Night Goblins. These types are not physically different "
"to each other, although all kinds of Goblin are liable to extreme variations "
"in size, so it is quite usual for a mob of Goblins to include some "
"individuals as much as twice the size of others. In this respect, where a "
"big Snotling becomes a Goblin and vice versa is debatable, though from an "
"Orc’s point of view it hardly matters as they’re all there to be bossed "
"about."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:75
msgid ""
"The majority of Goblins living in open areas, most notably in the Badlands "
"and Dark Lands, are Common Goblins or just ordinary Gobbos. They are as "
"common as muck throughout the hills, valleys and plains of the Old World and "
"beyond. We quite cheerfully refer to all the different kinds of Goblins as "
"Goblins, but where this might prove confusing we call ordinary Common "
"Goblins just that ... Common Goblins. And ain’t they just!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Common Goblins ride Giant Wolves much as humans ride horses. Not only are "
"these large and dangerous creatures ridden by individual Goblins, but "
"chariots and carts may be pulled by several Giant Wolves harnessed together. "
"Giant Wolves are vicious creatures with slavering fangs and sharp claws, "
"quite often more dangerous than their Goblin riders. They are faster than "
"horses too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:89
msgid ""
"Goblin Wolf Riders commonly raid and pillage ahead of advancing Goblin "
"hordes, scouring the countryside for signs of enemy troop movements. On the "
"battlefield they harry the flanks of enemy units and chase down those who’ve "
"fled braver greenskins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:97
msgid ""
"Night Goblins are adapted to life underground where they subsist on fungi, "
"cave squigs, beetles and bits of each other.  They live under the mountains "
"throughout the Old World and Southlands in tunnels and caverns that are cool "
"and dark. Night Goblins have a strong aversion to daylight and when forced "
"above ground wear black or very dark enveloping robes to protect themselves "
"from the sun’s rays."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "Goblin army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$goblins.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:120
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[goblins,†1]]1. Goblins"
msgstr "[[goblins,†1]]1. Gobelins"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:122
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:123
msgid ""
"A Goblin unit is allowed to shoot as if it had bows but its range is reduced "
"to 15cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:127
msgid ""
"Up to two units per full 1000 points can be replaced by Squig Herds while "
"still counting for the Goblin min/max value. Note that these units still "
"count for min/max value of Squig Herds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:133
msgid ""
"When trying to issue an order to a unit of Trolls or to a brigade that "
"contains a unit of Trolls, any Command penalty applied for distance between "
"the character and the Troll unit is always doubled. So at 20cm no penalty "
"applies, at 40cm −2, at 60cm −4, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:140
msgid ""
"Trolls can regenerate wounds – in each round of combat after whole stands "
"have been removed Trolls automatically regenerate one outstanding hit. If no "
"hits are left over after removing whole stands then regeneration has no "
"effect. Regenerated hits still count towards the combat result for the round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wolf-riders,†3]]3. Wolf Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:146
msgid ""
"The Wolf Riders have a shooting range of 15cm and 360° vision – stands in "
"this unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading "
"and shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit "
"still needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Les Chevaucheurs de Loups ont une portée de tir de 15cm et une vision à 360° "
"- c'est-à-dire que les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer une ligne de vue "
"depuis n'importe quel bord de leur socle, ceci afin d'éviter ou de tirer, "
"incluant le tir sur les ennemis en charge. Notez que l'unité a tout de même "
"besoin d'avoir une Ligne de Vue depuis son bord avant pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pump-wagon,†4]]4. Pump Wagon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:155
msgid ""
"The Pump Wagon doesn’t move in Command phase by initiative or by successful "
"orders. Instead it always moves once up to 1D6 × 10cm. This move is "
"automatic, requires no Command roll, and happens at any time during the "
"Command phase but may not interrupt a character giving orders or units "
"moving (including other Pump Wagons). This gives the Pump Wagon a movement "
"of between 10cm and 60cm each turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:162
msgid ""
"In the combat round a Pump Wagon receives D6 attacks. This is in addition to "
"any additional attacks it receives for charging enemy in the open and for "
"being a chariot. When charged or after retreating as a result of combat, its "
"attacks are halved to D3. Roll to determine the number of attacks an every "
"round of combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:170
msgid ""
"A Pump Wagon cannot be driven back by shooting and does not roll for drive "
"backs. Pump Wagons ignore confusion. A Pump Wagon cannot be brigaded with "
"other units; not even another Pump Wagons, and characters cannot join it. "
"The enemy does not gain Victory points for a destroyed Pump Wagon and a Pump "
"Wagon does not count towards the Goblin army’s break value in any way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:171
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant,†5]]5. Giant"
msgstr "[[giant,†5]]5. Géant"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[doom-diver,†6]]6. Doom Diver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:176
msgid ""
"The Doom Diver has a range of 60cm and a unit hit by a Doom Diver is allowed "
"to make its normal armour save."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:179
msgid ""
"Doom Divers shoot at such a high trajectory that they cannot shoot at "
"charging enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[spear-chukka,†7]]7. Spear Chukka"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:181
msgid ""
"The Spear Chukka is a xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#bolt-"
"thrower[Bolt Thrower]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wolf-chariot,†8]]8. Wolf Chariot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:184
msgid "A General, Hero or Wizard can ride a Wolf Chariot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:186
msgid "The character riding a chariot adds +1 to his Attacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wyvern,†9]]9. Wyvern"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:188
msgid "Characters may ride Wyverns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:192
msgid ""
"A Wyvern can fly increasing its rider’s movement from 60cm to 100cm, and it "
"adds +2 Attacks to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:195
msgid "A unit that includes a Wyvern rider causes terror in its enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:199
#, no-wrap
msgid "Goblin spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mork Save Uz!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:208
msgid ""
"_The Shaman summons the power of Mork to protect the greenskins from the "
"enemy._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:214
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any friendly unit within 30cm of the Shaman. The "
"unit gains a 5+ save worked out in the usual manner until the beginning of "
"their next turn. If the unit already has a saving roll then it can choose "
"which one to make, but may not take both."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:216
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gerroff!!!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:219
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:210
msgid "[.cost]#5+ to cast# [.points]#Range 60cm#"
msgstr "[.cost]#5+ pour lancer# [.points]#Portée 60cm#"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:222
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:213
msgid ""
"_The voice of Gork booms out across the battlefield driving back his foes "
"with a rancid gale force yell._"
msgstr ""
"_La voix de Gork tonne sur le champ de bataille et repousse ses ennemis d’un "
"cri surpuissant._"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:226
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:178
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:217
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any unengaged enemy unit within range regardless "
"of whether the Shaman can see it or not. The spell cannot be cast on a unit "
"engaged in combat."
msgstr ""
"Ce sort peut être lancé sur une unité ennemie à portée du Chaman, qu’il "
"puisse la voir ou non, mais pas sur une unité engagée au combat."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:233
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The enemy unit is driven back 1D6 x 5cm towards its own table edge. This "
#| "is treated in the same way as a drive back from shooting, except that the "
#| "direction is established by determining the shortest route to the table "
#| "edge. A unit cannot be routed by a drive back from a Gerroff spell. If "
#| "the unit leaves the table edge it must roll as described in the main "
#| "Warmaster rules."
msgid ""
"The enemy unit is driven back 1D6 × 5cm towards its own table edge. This is "
"treated in the same way as a drive back from shooting, except that the "
"direction is established by determining the shortest route to the table "
"edge. A unit cannot be routed by a drive back from a Gerroff spell. If the "
"unit leaves the table edge it must roll as described in the main Warmaster "
"rules."
msgstr ""
"L’unité ennemie est repoussée par le hurlement de 1D6 x 5cm vers son bord de "
"table, comme pour un tir ordinaire, sauf que sa direction est celle du "
"chemin le plus court vers le bord de table. Une unité ne peut pas être "
"dispersée suite à un repoussement causé par ce sort. Si l’unité quitte la "
"table, elle doit effectuer un jet comme indiqué dans les règles de base de "
"Warmaster."

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:235
#, no-wrap
msgid "Brain Busta"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:241
msgid ""
"_A fearsome bolt of pure Waaagh! energy issues from the Shaman’s "
"outstretched hand and strikes an enemy unit._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:248
msgid ""
"The Shaman must be able to see his target to use this spell and it cannot be "
"directed at a unit engaged in combat. Brain Busta is treated like three "
"ordinary shooting attacks except that armour saves have no effect (all "
"targets count as having no armour).  A unit can be driven back by Brain "
"Busta as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Waaagh!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:256
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:232
msgid ""
"_The shaman summons the power of the mighty Waaagh! to invigorate the "
"greenskins._"
msgstr ""
"_Le chaman invoque la puissance de la grande Waaagh ! pour encourager les "
"peaux vertes._"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:262
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on a friendly unit of Goblins engaged in combat; "
"including Squig Herds, Wolf Riders, Wolf Chariots and Pump Wagons but not "
"Trolls, Giants or other non-greenskins.  The spell can be cast regardless of "
"whether the Shaman can see the target or not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:266
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:242
msgid ""
"The spell lasts for the duration of the following Combat phase.  Every stand "
"in the unit, including characters that have joined the unit, adds +1 to its "
"Attacks value."
msgstr ""
"Le sort dure toute la prochaine phase de combat.  Chaque socle de l’unité, y "
"compris les socles de Personnages qui l’ont rejointe, ajoute +1 à sa valeur "
"d’Attaques."
